# FDAT - Flight Data Acquisition and Telemetry

A personal project to build a small flight data acquisition system using an ESP32-S3.

The idea is to collect data from a few sensors, store it on an SD card, and eventually transmit it to a computer for live monitoring. I'm mainly doing this to get more experience with embedded programming, electronics, and working with sensors.

## Hardware

- **ESP32-S3 SuperMini** - Main microcontroller
- **BMP388** - Barometric pressure and temperature
- **LSM6DSOX** - Accelerometer and gyroscope
- **INA219** - Voltage and current monitoring
- **MicroSD module** - Data logging

## Software

- C++ (Arduino framework)
- PlatformIO / VS Code
- Python for data analysis and visualization

## Goals

The first goal is to get each sensor working individually and understand how it communicates with the ESP32.

Once that's done, I'll combine everything into a single system that can sample data at set frequencies, timestamp measurements, and save them to an SD card.

After that, I'd like to add live telemetry and a simple Python interface to visualize the data.

## Progress

- [x] Set up ESP32-S3 with PlatformIO
- [x] Basic GPIO and onboard LED testing
- [ ] Read pressure and temperature from BMP388
- [ ] Read acceleration and angular velocity from LSM6DSOX
- [ ] Integrate INA219
- [ ] Implement timestamps and consistent sampling
- [ ] Log sensor data to microSD
- [ ] Send data to PC
- [ ] Visualize data using Python
- [ ] Design and print an enclosure
- [ ] Test the complete system

## Notes

I'm building this incrementally rather than trying to connect and program everything at once. Each component will be tested separately before integration.

I'll update this README as the project progresses.